{"ticker":"LUMINO","symbol":"LUMINO","instrumentId":3204014,"name":"Lumino Industries Ltd","industry":"NSE-Electrical-Power/Equipmt","about":"\"Lumino Industries operates two principal segments: manufacturing and engineering, procurement and construction (EPC). Its manufacturing portfolio includes conductors, cables and house wires used in power transmission, distribution, industrial systems and buildings. The company has one manufacturing facility in Howrah, West Bengal, and serves India as well as international markets.\n\nIts EPC business undertakes power transmission and distribution networks, EHV substations, HTLS reconductoring, railway electrification, solar power projects and water management. These services support utilities, infrastructure developers and public-sector projects. Lumino provides turnkey project execution, combining engineering, procurement, construction and quality control for energy and infrastructure applications. The projects strengthen infrastructure.\"","website":"www.luminoindustries.com","location":null,"exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:38:54.623Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":93.39,"changePct":-3.7712519319938145,"week52High":114.95,"week52Low":0},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹2,844 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹1,895 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"85,275,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"31"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"34,848,976"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.00%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"3.12"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"2.2"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"4.0%"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"-0.42"},{"label":"Beta","value":"1.77"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"86%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"12.12"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"14–15"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"21.9%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"6.41"},{"label":"Volume","value":"2,130,057"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"7,088,115"},{"label